Requirement Analysis Phase – PocketSmart AI
The Requirement Analysis Phase identifies what the PocketSmart AI system needs to provide to users. The main goal is to understand user needs and define the features required to develop a useful Smart Budget & Recommendation Assistant.
Functional Requirements
User Registration/Login – Users can create an account and securely log in.
Income Management – Users can enter and update their monthly income.
Expense Tracking – Users can record their daily expenses.
Expense Categorization – Expenses can be divided into food, travel, shopping, bills, etc.
Budget Creation – Users can set monthly or category-wise budgets.
Budget Monitoring – The system tracks spending against the set budget.
AI Recommendations – PocketSmart suggests suitable spending and saving options based on the user's budget.
Spending Alerts – Users receive alerts when their spending approaches or exceeds the budget.
Reports & Analysis – The system provides summaries of income, expenses, savings, and spending patterns.
Savings Goals – Users can create and track specific savings goals.
Non-Functional Requirements
Easy to use: Simple and user-friendly interface.
Security: User financial information should be protected.
Performance: Recommendations and calculations should be generated quickly.
Reliability: Data should be stored accurately.
Scalability: The system should support more users and features in the future.
Hardware & Software Requirements
Hardware: Smartphone/Computer, internet connection, sufficient storage.
Software: Frontend, backend/database, AI or recommendation module, and a web/mobile browser or application.
Expected Outcome
PocketSmart AI should help users understand their spending, manage their budget, reduce unnecessary expenses, and make better financial decisions through personalized recommendations.
